      "message": "[error] Line 108: 🔴 This SSRC tuple is not a legacy-only packet marker: SSRCs are opaque 32-bit values, so a standards-compliant one-SSRC REMB can legitimately contain sender `0x12345678` and feedback `0x2345678b`. If its absolute bitrate is `0x6803` or `0x7378`, this check still labels it as a relative command and `VideoRtpSession` applies a 15%/increase adjustment instead of the requested target. The new test only uses different SSRCs for the standard case. Gate legacy interpretation on peer/session capability or another unambiguous legacy context, and add a regression test for a standard packet with this exact tuple.",
